![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5720acc-d2ac-4fac-ab4f-18a63101376a)

We have a bunch of client-side preferences scattered around the client, and are likely to add more in the future.
This PR adds a common store for all those preferences, and a preference Page which is generated from the store,
in order for local preferences to be more transparent to users.

It also makes some small cleanup changes to the user preference Page, reusing the UserPreferencesElement where possible, instead of recreating it in multiple places.

**Example of how to define a local preference**

In the new store, local preferences can be defined as follows:

```ts
    const hideSelectionQueryBreakWarning = useLocalPreference(allPreferences, preferenceRefsById, {
        id: "hide-selection-query-break-warning",
        default: false,
        name: "Hide history 'select all' warning",
        description:
            "Do not show the warning that pops up when manually modifying a 'select all' selection in the history",
    });
```

The preference can be then used as follows:

```ts
const { hideSelectionQueryBreakWarning } = useLocalPreferences();

hideSelectionQueryBreakWarning.value = true;
```
In this example the type is inferred from the default value, but more complex types with type constraints can also be defined:

```ts
    const preferredListViewMode = useLocalPreference(allPreferences, preferenceRefsById, {
        id: "preferred-list-view-mode",
        default: "grid" as ListViewMode,
        name: "Preferred List View Mode",
        description: "If Lists should be displayed as a grid, or list of items",
        type: {
            option: true,
            options: [
                { label: "Grid", value: "grid" },
                { label: "List", value: "list" },
            ],
        },
    });
```

```ts
   const workflowEditorMaxUndoActions = useLocalPreference(allPreferences, preferenceRefsById, {
        id: "workflow-editor-max-undo-actions",
        category: workflowEditorCategory,
        default: 100,
        name: "Max Undo Actions",
        description: "How many steps are undoable in the workflow editor. Setting this lower saves resources",
        type: {
            number: true,
            range: {
                min: 10,
                max: 10000,
            },
            step: 1,
        },
    });
```

The type constraints are not just used to render the user facing local preference page, but also enforced on a ref level.
The ref which is returned by `useLocalPreferences()` is guaranteed to follow these constraints.

