/ahmedhamidawan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmedhamidawan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmedhamidawan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmedhamidawan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmedhamidawan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmedhamidawan/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"body":"This adds a **graph view** to the workflow invocation summary, which utilizes the workflow editor canvas and original workflow structure, and instead of showing step details on each step node, it shows the job states for the steps. Clicking on a step expands the details for the invocation step.

The `useInvocationGraph` composable loads the graph onto the readonly editor based on the original workflow id and invocation object; and the step info is loaded via the `step_jobs_summary` api route.

| An example invocation overview |
| ---------------- |
| ![image](https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/88d4b408-4308-42ff-83e7-8ce60b758f6d) |

## Sample Workflow Run:

https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/32dc87c5-7cfc-47c5-8fe4-5c042cdc4a83

# Invocation View Header:
This also adds a header with details about the invocation:
![image](https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/fc2fed46-aaf8-46c2-b452-75d923dad414)

### Older (alternative?) Implementation:
With a Card containing everything inline:
![image](https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/3ec283db-0983-4713-81a1-790412998589)

# Hide and Show steps as needed:
To view multiple individual steps at the same time (without the graph getting in the way), users can hide/show steps like so:

https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/74604985-5645-4384-972d-97516baa68f9

# Invocations List Change: Route to invocation instead of only expanding table rows
This change allows you to click an invocation workflow name and route to the dedicated full page (center-panel) summary for the invocation, while you can still expand it within the table by clicking on the expand details icon in the first column:

## Before:

https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/a9d9d968-d86d-4a0a-b112-a4df8f493c75

## Now:

https://github.com/galaxyproject/galaxy/assets/78516064/8f9585de-999e-4115-8832-89f8d98ba544

